# Stroke License

Copyright (c) 2026 Nischal Dahal

You may do whatever you want with the Stroke source code and other source
files (from here on referred to as the "Stroke Source"), with the following
restrictions:

- If you publish any work derived from the Stroke Source, you must make it
  apparent in some way that it is derived from Stroke.
- If you have created an executable program (from here on called "Your
  Program") compiled from some source code and/or other source files (from
  here on called "Your Source"), and if Your Source includes files or source
  code copied or derived from the Stroke Source, then you may only publish
  Your Program under the following conditions:
	- Your Program does not contain any malware or hidden malicious content.
	- You may not charge users money for Your Program, and Your Source must
	  contain the monetization systems present in the Stroke Source,
	  including the license-key activation, trial period tracking, and
	  payment system, without any alterations. All of these systems must be
	  active and working as intended in Your Program, and payments made
	  through them must go to the original author of Stroke. That is unless
	  Your Source features substantial improvements or additions to the
	  Stroke Source, such that Your Source should be considered its own,
	  derivative work, separate from the Stroke Source. Removing, bypassing,
	  or replacing the monetization systems, renaming or restyling the app,
	  or other cosmetic changes do not by themselves count as substantial
	  improvements or additions.
	- Your Program is not published under the name "Stroke", or under a name
	  or icon so similar to Stroke's that users could mistake Your Program
	  for Stroke.

THE STROKE SOURCE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
